{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"git-quick","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Git Quick Actions","description":"Status, pull, push, commit, branch, stash, log and blame as commands. Everything runs visibly in the terminal.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Git"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:gitQuick.status","onCommand:gitQuick.pull","onCommand:gitQuick.push","onCommand:gitQuick.fetch","onCommand:gitQuick.commit","onCommand:gitQuick.commitAll","onCommand:gitQuick.amend","onCommand:gitQuick.undoCommit","onCommand:gitQuick.newBranch","onCommand:gitQuick.switchBranch","onCommand:gitQuick.branches","onCommand:gitQuick.stash","onCommand:gitQuick.stashPop","onCommand:gitQuick.log","onCommand:gitQuick.diff","onCommand:gitQuick.diffStaged","onCommand:gitQuick.discardUnstaged","onCommand:gitQuick.tag","onCommand:gitQuick.tags","onCommand:gitQuick.remotes","onCommand:gitQuick.fileHistory","onCommand:gitQuick.blameFile"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"gitQuick.status","title":"Status","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.pull","title":"Pull","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.push","title":"Push","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.fetch","title":"Fetch All","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.commit","title":"Commit Staged...","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.commitAll","title":"Stage All and Commit...","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.amend","title":"Amend Last Commit","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.undoCommit","title":"Undo Last Commit (Keep Changes)","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.newBranch","title":"New Branch...","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.switchBranch","title":"Switch Branch...","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.branches","title":"List Branches","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.stash","title":"Stash Changes","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.stashPop","title":"Pop Stash","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.log","title":"Show Log Graph","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.diff","title":"Show Diff","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.diffStaged","title":"Show Staged Diff","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.discardUnstaged","title":"Discard Unstaged Changes","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.tag","title":"Create Tag...","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.tags","title":"List Tags","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.remotes","title":"Show Remotes","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.fileHistory","title":"History of This File","category":"Git Quick Actions"},{"command":"gitQuick.blameFile","title":"Blame This File","category":"Git Quick Actions"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Git Quick Actions: the git commands you use all day, one command away. Everything runs visibly in the terminal.\r\n\r\n// Double quotes work in cmd, PowerShell and Bash. Anything a shell would treat specially inside them is refused.\r\nconst q = (s) => {\r\n  const t = String(s);\r\n  if (/[\"$`\\\\!%^]/.test(t)) throw new Error('That text has a character that is not safe to type into a shell (double quote, dollar, backtick, backslash, !, %, ^). Use the terminal for it.');\r\n  return '\"' + t + '\"';\r\n};\r\n/** Paths are written with forward slashes, which every shell and git accept. */\r\nconst qpath = (p) => q(String(p).replace(/\\\\/g, '/'));\r\n\r\n/** A commit message must be one line without anything a shell would treat specially. */\r\nfunction commitCommand(message, all) {\r\n  const m = String(message).trim();\r\n  if (!m) throw new Error('A commit message cannot be empty.');\r\n  if (/[\\r\\n]/.test(m)) throw new Error('Use a one line message here.');\r\n  return (all ? 'git add -A && ' : '') + 'git commit -m ' + q(m);\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction branchName(s) {\r\n  const b = String(s).trim().replace(/\\s+/g, '-');\r\n  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9._\\/-]+$/.test(b) || b.startsWith('-') || b.includes('..') || b.endsWith('/') || b.endsWith('.lock')) throw new Error('That is not a good branch name. Use letters, digits, dots, dashes and slashes.');\r\n  return b;\r\n}\r\n\r\nexports._test = { q, qpath, commitCommand, branchName };\r\n\r\nexports.activate = function (context) {\r\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\r\n  const run = (cmd) => ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\r\n  const simple = {\r\n    'gitQuick.status': 'git status -sb', 'gitQuick.pull': 'git pull --ff-only', 'gitQuick.push': 'git push', 'gitQuick.fetch': 'git fetch --all --prune',\r\n    'gitQuick.log': 'git log --oneline --graph --decorate -20', 'gitQuick.diff': 'git diff', 'gitQuick.diffStaged': 'git diff --staged', 'gitQuick.stash': 'git stash push -u',\r\n    'gitQuick.stashPop': 'git stash pop', 'gitQuick.undoCommit': 'git reset --soft HEAD~1', 'gitQuick.discardUnstaged': null, 'gitQuick.branches': 'git branch -vv',\r\n    'gitQuick.remotes': 'git remote -v', 'gitQuick.amend': 'git commit --amend --no-edit', 'gitQuick.tags': 'git tag --sort=-creatordate | head -20',\r\n  };\r\n  for (const [id, cmd] of Object.entries(simple)) {\r\n    if (cmd) reg(id, () => run(cmd));\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  reg('gitQuick.discardUnstaged', async () => {\r\n    if (await ferrum.window.confirm('Discard every change that is not staged? This cannot be undone.', 'Discard')) await run('git restore .');\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.commit', async () => {\r\n    const m = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Commit message (staged changes)', placeholder: 'Fix the thing' });\r\n    if (m === undefined) return;\r\n    try { await run(commitCommand(m, false)); } catch (e) { ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn'); }\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.commitAll', async () => {\r\n    const m = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Commit message (stages everything first)', placeholder: 'Fix the thing' });\r\n    if (m === undefined) return;\r\n    try { await run(commitCommand(m, true)); } catch (e) { ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn'); }\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.newBranch', async () => {\r\n    const n = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'New branch name', placeholder: 'feature/my-change' });\r\n    if (n === undefined) return;\r\n    try { await run('git switch -c ' + q(branchName(n))); } catch (e) { ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn'); }\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.switchBranch', async () => {\r\n    const n = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Switch to which branch?', placeholder: 'main' });\r\n    if (n === undefined) return;\r\n    try { await run('git switch ' + q(branchName(n))); } catch (e) { ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn'); }\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.tag', async () => {\r\n    const n = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Tag name', placeholder: 'v1.0.0' });\r\n    if (n === undefined) return;\r\n    try { await run('git tag ' + q(branchName(n))); } catch (e) { ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'warn'); }\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.fileHistory', async () => {\r\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n    if (!doc || !doc.path) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a saved file first.', 'warn');\r\n    await run('git log --follow --oneline -- ' + qpath(doc.path));\r\n  });\r\n  reg('gitQuick.blameFile', async () => {\r\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n    if (!doc || !doc.path) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a saved file first.', 'warn');\r\n    await run('git blame ' + qpath(doc.path));\r\n  });\r\n};\r\n\r\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\r\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Git Quick Actions\n\nThe git commands you type every day, in the command palette (prefix \"Git Quick\"). They run **in the terminal, in front of you**, so nothing is hidden, and you can edit the command before pressing Enter if you want.\n\n- Status, pull (fast-forward only), push, fetch all with prune.\n- Commit staged, stage everything and commit, amend, undo the last commit but keep the changes.\n- New branch, switch branch, list branches.\n- Stash and pop, log graph, diff, staged diff, tags, remotes.\n- History and blame of the open file.\n- **Discard Unstaged Changes** asks first.\n\nMessages and names are checked so nothing special (quotes, dollar signs, backticks) reaches the shell.\n\n## Permissions\n**terminal**, to type commands into the terminal.\n"}}}